{
  "case_id": "2009-08-678",
  "document_hash": "45722f921809ce096bb8724e229dfd9592197bb6e77529be5f4857931a832460",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Supreme Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-678",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "45722f921809ce096bb8724e229dfd9592197bb6e77529be5f4857931a832460",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45722f921809-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:05 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Randall L. Allen",
      "case_id": "2009-08-678",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "45722f921809ce096bb8724e229dfd9592197bb6e77529be5f4857931a832460",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45722f921809-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Allen: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: For well over a century this Court has recognized the importance of the attorney-client privilege."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Randall L. Allen",
      "case_id": "2009-08-678",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "45722f921809ce096bb8724e229dfd9592197bb6e77529be5f4857931a832460",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45722f921809-0000-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In Hunt v. Blackburn in 1888, the Court clearly states that the seal of secrecy upon communications between client and attorney is founded upon the necessity, in the interest of justice, that the aid and advice of persons having knowledge and skill in the practice of law provide that advice in a manner that is safely and readily available and, importantly, free from the consequences or apprehension of disclosure."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-678",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "45722f921809ce096bb8724e229dfd9592197bb6e77529be5f4857931a832460",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45722f921809-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Mr. Allen, except for the fact that you and I are lawyers, do you really think that the -- that confidentiality right is any more important to the proper functioning of society than, let's say, the protection of trade secrets?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Allen",
      "case_id": "2009-08-678",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "45722f921809ce096bb8724e229dfd9592197bb6e77529be5f4857931a832460",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45722f921809-0000-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The incremental erosion of the rule is going to lessen the value of the privilege."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Allen",
      "case_id": "2009-08-678",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "45722f921809ce096bb8724e229dfd9592197bb6e77529be5f4857931a832460",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45722f921809-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We have asked that the Court address, in this instance, the question presented having to do with only waiver cases."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-678",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "45722f921809ce096bb8724e229dfd9592197bb6e77529be5f4857931a832460",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45722f921809-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So -- but your position logically would apply to everything, wouldn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-678",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "45722f921809ce096bb8724e229dfd9592197bb6e77529be5f4857931a832460",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45722f921809-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is there any sensible line between an invocation of the privilege, denied, and a holding that the privilege has been waived?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Resnik",
      "case_id": "2009-08-678",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "45722f921809ce096bb8724e229dfd9592197bb6e77529be5f4857931a832460",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45722f921809-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We do not extend the -- the rule that we advocate to work product in the -- in the broad sense."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Edwin S. Kneedler",
      "case_id": "2009-08-678",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "45722f921809ce096bb8724e229dfd9592197bb6e77529be5f4857931a832460",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45722f921809-0002-0000",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the last 15 years, this Court, in applying the principles of Cohen, has repeatedly stressed that a necessary requirement is that the order involved and the issues implicated be important and, particularly, that the issues be so important as to outweigh the values served by the important and usual rule of a final judgment requirement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Edwin S. Kneedler",
      "case_id": "2009-08-678",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "45722f921809ce096bb8724e229dfd9592197bb6e77529be5f4857931a832460",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45722f921809-0002-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When you give advice to a government agency, you don't call that the attorney-client privilege. You call it a governmental privilege, a deliberative privilege, all these other things."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-678",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "45722f921809ce096bb8724e229dfd9592197bb6e77529be5f4857931a832460",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45722f921809-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Sotomayor asked about -- about a test for importance, and the Court, in its recent decision in Will, tried to summarize what -- what it has been driving at over the last 15 years on this importance prong and whether the importance outweighs the -- the final judgment values."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Randall L. Allen",
      "case_id": "2009-08-678",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "45722f921809ce096bb8724e229dfd9592197bb6e77529be5f4857931a832460",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45722f921809-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I would like to address the question that Justice Alito raised with regard to whether or not an appeal of a collateral issue dealing with waiver or privilege would stay the litigation. The answer is it does not."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-678",
      "confidence": 0.98,
      "document_hash": "45722f921809ce096bb8724e229dfd9592197bb6e77529be5f4857931a832460",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45722f921809-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
